---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends analytics to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink>. This data includes app use,
      purchases, crashes, performance, app and device details, and settings
      details. Settings details include accessibility settings, color scheme,
      language, layout direction, and region. The data helps improve the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      A random ID is made for each install. It stays the same until the app's
      data is reset or the app is deleted. The ID itself is not sent. The app
      sends letters and numbers made from it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics can be turned off in the app's settings. No new analytics are
      sent after that. Data already sent is not deleted. There is no set
      deletion date. Sent records have no name, email, or other detail that ties
      them to a person. One person's records cannot be found and deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck must protect this data at least as well as this policy and
      Apple's rules require.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      A content report is an email. It includes the reason, round ID, app
      version, build number, and the reporter's email address. The drawing is
      included only if the reporter attaches it. The report is used to review
      the reported content.
    </p>
    <p>
      Report emails are kept in the support inbox. To remove one, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address that sent it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No one uses {APP_NAME} to track activity on other websites or in other
      companies' apps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Important changes to this policy are posted here.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
